@ 15 - Eskimo-Aleut
# citation: The following phonological reconstruction of Proto-Eskimo-Aleut is adapted from Wikipedia. It is noted that *n and *nʲ may not have been distinct phonemes; the article cites Fortescue mentioning that Sirilenski Eskimo has instances of initial /j/ whereas others have /n/; that *c *sʲ may have been either fricatives (*s *sʲ) or affricates (*ts *tsʲ), the source being unclear; and that *ɬ may have actually arisen from *l + plosive combinations. (From Wikipedia contributors (2013), “Proto-Eskimo–Aleut language”. Wikipedia, the Free Encyclopedia.